    "long_instructions": "\r\nIn an era where AI tools can generate code quickly, assessment must shift from evaluating what students build to understanding how they build it.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Redefining “Success” in Coding\r\n\r\nWhen AI can produce working features or write code, evaluating only the final product is no longer sufficient.\r\n\r\nThis capstone is designed as a process-oriented experience, emphasizing:\r\n- Decision-making\r\n- Testing\r\n- Iteration and refinement\r\n- Evaluating AI Judgment\r\n\r\n\r\nA student’s final app is only one part of their work.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #e4e2f8; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; margin: 20px 0px;\"> <p style=\"font-weight: bold; font-size: 12pt;\">Simplicity + Reasoning &gt; Complexity + Confusion</p> </div>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWatch the video below to learn about assessment in the age of AI.  \r\n"
